.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
.TH OCTA-PCM-PEAK-CHECK 1 "" "OCTA-CAPTURE @PROJECT_VERSION@" "OCTA-CAPTURE Manual"
.SH NAME
octa\-pcm\-peak\-check \- check kernel peak retention with quiet channel tags
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBocta-pcm-peak-check\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Developer check using exclusive PCM/meter access on hw:CARD=OCTACAPTURE.
It plays very quiet positive channel tags and zeros, then checks the retained
playback peaks and their clearing behavior.
This writes real PCM output and must not run alongside other meter/audio clients.
It uses the current hardware rate and does not establish calibrated physical gain.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success; nonzero indicates a usage, device or operation error.
.SH SEE ALSO
octa-capture(1), octa-status(1), octa-preset(1)
